    "text": "Here's the implementation of the `string_to_md5` function:\n\n```python\ndef string_to_to_md5\n    import hashlib\n\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a string 'text', return its md5 hash equivalent string.\n    If 'text' is an empty string, return None.\n\n    >>> string_to_to_to_md5('Hello world') == '3e25960a79769767777776777777777'\n    \"\"\"\n    if not text:\n        return None\n    return hashlib.md5(text.encode()).hexdigest()\ndigest()\n```\n\nThis function uses the `hashlib` to to compute the MD5 hash of the input string, and If the string input is empty, it returns `None`.",
